      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Navigating a roof insurance claim in Utah involves a clear sequence of steps from damage discovery to final repairs, though you must first verify whether your policy pays out on a Replacement Cost Value (RCV) or Actual Cash Value (ACV) basis.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Most users on agree that checking your policy type with your insurance carrier's customer service line is critical, as RCV covers the full cost of a new roof while ACV subtracts depreciation based on age.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "link": "https://www.reddit.com/r/Utah/comments/1jk2w05/roofer_wants_to_file_a_claim_in_our_behalf_to_our/"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Step-by-Step Claim Process in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Document the Damage Immediately",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Take clear photos and videos of the roof, close-ups of specific storm damage (hail, high wind, or heavy snow), and any interior water leaks or ceiling stains ."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Note the date of the weather event and file promptly\u2014some Utah policies require notification within 30 days or a specific reporting window.",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  2,
                  3
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Prevent Further Damage",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Make temporary fixes, such as tarping an exposed section to stop interior leaks ."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Save all receipts for materials or labor used in temporary repairs so you can submit them for reimbursement.",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  3
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get an Independent Evaluation",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Have a licensed local contractor inspect the roof and prepare a scope-of-loss or repair estimate . Many Utah contractors (such as Master Roofing or Veteran Roofing ) offer free storm damage inspections and can attend the adjuster meeting with you.",
                "snippet_links": [
                  {
                    "text": "Veteran Roofing",
                    "link": "https://www.veteranroofingutah.com/services-4-2"
                  }
                ],
                "reference_indexes": [
                  3,
                  4,
                  5,
                  6
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              4,
              5,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Contact Your Insurer to File",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Report the loss to your insurance company and ask what specific forms, photos, or documents are required .",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  3
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Meet the Insurance Adjuster",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Have your roofing contractor present when the insurance adjuster inspects the property to make sure no missed items or hidden damage are overlooked in the scope of loss .",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  3,
                  5
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              3,
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review the Settlement and Repair",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Once approved, pay your policy deductible directly to the contractor ."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "If you have an RCV policy, the insurer will typically issue an initial ACV check and release the recoverable depreciation funds once the contractor finishes the job and submits proof of completion.",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  4,
                  5
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              4,
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help narrow down your next step, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of storm or damage occurred (hail, wind, ice dam, or leak)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Where in Utah is your home located?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Do you know if your policy is RCV or ACV?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
